WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
We differentiate between factual statements,
which describe states of affairs,

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.480
or how things are, and evaluative
statements, which express value or

3
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
obligation, dictating how things ought to
be.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.800
These statements use a spectrum of
terminology.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.280
Thin terms, like right or wrong, are
purely evaluative.

6
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.140
Thick terms, such as courage, contain both
a descriptive component and an

7
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.940
evaluative judgment. Identifying whether a
premise is factual or evaluative,

8
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.760
determines the logical limits of the
resulting argument.
